      "dom_id": "question-12786",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use the difference of squares method to solve the equation $p$ is $4{p}^{2}=25.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and collect the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{p}^{2} & =25 \\\\ 4{p}^{2}-25 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the difference of squares formula, we factor the left-hand side of our quadratic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{p}^{2}-25 & =0 \\\\ (2p)^{2}-{5}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (2p-5)(2p+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the zero product rule, we have\n\n$$\n2p-5=0\\,\\text{or}\\,2p+5=0.\n$$\n\nThen, we solve each equation separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-5 & =0 & \\, & \\, & 2p+5 & =0 \\\\ 2p & =5 & \\, & \\, & 2p & =-5 \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{2} & \\, & \\, & p & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p=-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2}.$ We can write this even more concisely as $p=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}.$",
